::ingredients

(yogurt, Greek) 2 cups
(cucumber) 3 inches
(dill) as needed
(garlic) 1 clove/teaspoon
(olive oil) 1tsp; optional extra in method
(acid) = (lemon juice) as needed -OR- (lime juice) as needed -OR- (vinegar) as needed
(salt) generous pinch in method
(pepper) small pinch in method

::equipment

(kitchen towel, clean)
(mortar and pestle)

::instructions

(cucumber) <grate, finely>
(dill) <chop>
(cucumber) <strain, thoroughly, clean kitchen towel>
(garlic) + (olive oil) <mash, mortar and pestle>
{tzatziki} = (yogurt) + (cucumber) + (dill) + (garlic) + (olive oil)
{tzatziki} + (acid) <squeeze, some lemon/lime or vinegar>
    + (salt) + (pepper)
Optional [
    {tzatziki} + (olive oil) extra
]
{tzatziki} <stir>
    <serve, favourite snack>

::story

A traditional greek dip that goes well with crackers, celery and carrots or in a greek gyro. Great for parties and sharing with your family friends. Can be eaten immediately after preparation or after a few hours of being in the fridge for enhanced flavor.

